The '''2026 Wakefield Metropolitan Borough Council election''' was held on 7 May 2026, alongside the [[2026 United Kingdom local elections|other local elections across the United Kingdom]] being held on the same day. All 63 members of [[Wakefield Metropolitan Borough Council]] were elected.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-01-16 |title=Wakefield Council confirms 2026 'all out' local election will go ahead as planned |url=https://www.wakefieldexpress.co.uk/news/people/wakefield-council-confirms-2026-all-out-local-election-will-go-ahead-as-planned-5478963 |access-date=2026-01-27 |website=Wakefield Express |language=en}}</ref>

== Background ==
In [[2024 Wakefield Metropolitan District Council election|2024]], Labour retained control of the council.<ref>{{Cite news |title=Wakefield result - Local Elections 2024 |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/election/2024/england/councils/E08000036 |access-date=2026-01-27 |work=BBC News |language=en-GB}}</ref>
Following ward boundary changes, all 63 seat on the council will be up for election.

